# ==========================================
# ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES TEMPLATE
# ==========================================
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file and rename it to '.env'
# 2. Fill in ONE of the provider blocks below.
# IMPORTANT: '.env' is gitignored — NEVER commit it.
#
# There is now a SINGLE agent stack: the Google ADK graph in
# machine_learning_engineering/adk_agent.py. It drives native Gemini OR an
# OpenAI / OpenAI-compatible endpoint, chosen purely by ROOT_AGENT_MODEL — no
# code change to switch providers. Web search (google_search) is Gemini-native,
# so it is only available on the Gemini path (auto-disabled otherwise).

# --- Option A: Native Google Gemini (AI Studio free tier) — web search ON ----
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. A bare `gemini-*` model id
# routes to native Gemini; the free AI Studio key works without Vertex/Cloud.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_ai_studio_key_here
GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=FALSE
ROOT_AGENT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Option B: OpenAI / OpenAI-compatible via ADK (LiteLlm) — web search OFF -
# Any non-`gemini` model id is wrapped in ADK's LiteLlm and reads API_KEY /
# API_BASE. Use the litellm provider prefix (e.g. `openai/…`). google_search is
# Gemini-only, so the analyst runs without web search on this path.
#   Real OpenAI:            API_BASE=https://api.openai.com/v1
#                           ROOT_AGENT_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o
#   University proxy (SAIA) / AI Studio OpenAI-compat base: point API_BASE there
#                           ROOT_AGENT_MODEL=openai/meta-llama-3.1-8b-instruct
# API_BASE=https://api.openai.com/v1
# API_KEY=your_openai_or_proxy_key_here
# ROOT_AGENT_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o
